  the page must be served ([38;5;153mpython3 -m http.server[39m, or anything equivalent) rather than opened from [38;5;153mfile://[39m, because
  module scripts are blocked by CORS on [38;5;153mfile://[39m.

  [1mError handling details:[0m a rule receives [38;5;153mvalues[field] ?? ""[39m, so a missing key behaves identically to an empty input —
  no [38;5;153mundefined[39m reaching rule code. Rules for a field stop at the first failure, so a field yields at most one message.
  Fields present in [38;5;153mvalues[39m but absent from [38;5;153mrules[39m are ignored, not rejected.

  [1mExplicit non-goals:[0m no second form is built, no DOM error rendering, no changes to [38;5;153msrc/[39m or [38;5;153mlogin()[39m.

  [1mTooling.[0m The repo has no test runner, linter, or formatter, so right now nothing can verify [38;5;153mvalidate()[39m except clicking
  the form. That's the weakest part of this plan — a reusable module with no tests is a module whose contract drifts.
  Setting this up is cheapest now, before the code exists. Node 18+ ships [38;5;153mnode:test[39m and [38;5;153mnode:assert[39m, so unit tests need
  zero dependencies: add [38;5;153m"type": "module"[39m and a [38;5;153m"test": "node --test"[39m script to [38;5;153mpackage.json[39m, plus [38;5;153mvalidation.test.js[39m.

